# Testing

**Invariant-centric procedure:** `.cursor/agent-kernel/protocols/testing.md` (Router loads when applicable).

## Pre-push

Run `./scripts/pre-push-changed.sh` during iteration or `./scripts/pre-push.sh` before merge to `main`. See `/pre-push-verify` skill.

## Layer expectations

| Layer | Tool | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| Node routes | Jest + supertest | Every route module gets a test file |
| Flutter domain/data | `flutter test` | Models, repos, datasources |
| Flutter UI | Widget tests | Extracted widgets + critical screens |
| Integration | `flutter test` integration dir | **Blocking in CI** — no `continue-on-error` |
| Journeys | Playwright (`e2e/`) | Full suite: **pre-uat-e2e.yml** (9 **duration-balanced** localhost shards from `e2e/scripts/shard-files.mjs`) post-merge to `main`; PR: **@smoke-ci** canary + **affected specs** (`ci-e2e-affected`, budget in `select-affected-specs.mjs`) when the diff is E2E-only; Flutter PRs still run the full stack + canary. Frozen specs listed in `e2e/scripts/frozen-e2e-specs.mjs`. |

## BDD (hybrid — no Cucumber runner)

- Gherkin specs: `flutter_app/test/bdd/features/`
- Playwright implementations: `e2e/playwright/tests/` with `/** @bdd <feature> */` comment
- New user journey → add Gherkin scenario **and** Playwright spec (or link debt issue)

## Flutter CI shards

Active Flutter unit/widget tests run in **six** manifest shards (`pet-profile`, `experience`, `core`, `auth`, `health`, `pet-care`) from `flutter_app/test/ci_shards.json`. `test/features/auth` stays in `perFileRoots` (coverage collector segfault when batched — not a flake).

## Semantics contract (page objects)

When a Playwright page object depends on a Flutter `Semantics(identifier: …)` (or label) that is not covered by an existing widget test, add a **semantics-contract** widget test in the mirrored `flutter_app/test/` path (pattern from #1235) in the same PR as the locator.

## E2E locator hygiene

- Assert **visibility**, not DOM absence — Flutter web may keep semantics nodes in the tree while off-screen (`expectHomeShellHidden` pattern).
- Scope assertions to the **target control/row**, not parent containers (drawer `innerText`, full-page regex) — avoids false positives from unrelated text (emails, IDs).
- Address **PR review comments in the same PR** when valid (must-fix / in-scope). Out-of-scope suggestions and deferred nits → GitHub issues per `docs/agent-efficiency/autonomous-pr-policy.md` §Debt issues (dedupe required). `/babysit-plus` and `/execute-plan` enforce this; plain `/babysit` defers to human judgment.

## Coverage

- Add tests before or during extraction, not after.
- New route → Jest; new widget → widget test in mirrored path.
- BDD: keep `@bdd` header titles **exact** match to Gherkin `Scenario:` lines; frozen scenarios use `@frozen` or live in excluded feature patterns (`manifest.json`).
- Pre-push: `node scripts/check_file_size.js`, `node e2e/scripts/check_bdd_coverage.js`, `bash scripts/check_frozen_domain_boundaries.sh`.
- Flutter CI shards: `flutter_app/test/ci_shards.json` is the only shard list — a new test directory must fall under a shard root (`node scripts/ci/flutter-shards.mjs check`, governance-blocking).
- Frozen domains: no org shard (frozen `testRoots` in `docs/engineering/frozen-domains/manifest.json` are excluded from the shard check); Jest active config excludes `server/test/organizations`; manual `scripts/test-frozen-domains.sh` only.
